{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1086485-the-importance-of-horror","id":1086485,"title":"The Importance of Horror.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-01T23:04:22-07:00","id":1086485,"title":"The Importance of Horror.","content":"I was having a bad day today. had a couple of arguments. Im not very into RPG's such as D&amp;D. i think they are WAY to lighthearted. too much of a &quot;Safe net.&quot; and i started to think about &quot;Why do i like horror so much.&quot; What drives me to try to Scare players, to push the envelopes...Well, i came up with this.<br /> I would like to see your thoughts on Why is horror important in our games. im not saying we have to keep it dry and terrifying 24/7 - Yes, i allow a jokes or funny situations- but this is my main view on the subject.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">i wanted to share you guys something. call it a moment of clarity, of WHy i love horror. and why i think horror is important in a game</span></span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You know why i jump so much into Horror?. Because, you know your players trust you. They trust you SO MUCH that they will put their own sanity int he line. Its EASY to disturb someone. Its EASY to make someone uncomfortable. You know what is hard? To keep them in the Rope of balancing both The game, their aspirations, and their love for their characters. In Fantasy, even High Fantasy. you will always land safe, you will Never loose anything. your character will only die because of their own stupidity. But there's no bigger consequences. Horror reminds us of our mortality. or How Horrifying the real world is...<br /> <br /> WE as StoryTellers -I hate the word DM- Tell stories, tell facts, tell bases and make enemies of our players characters. You know why? Because of the Outcome. Its So much rewarding to know that they will face Impossible Peril with nothing else but their guts and intelligence. Just That...To be able to see down into the Darkness and say &quot;I MADE IT THROUGH!&quot;. And to know that they trust you ENOUGH, not to cross the boundaries. Its SO easy to cross Lines, to use X subject that you know that triggers people..But its SO hard to give them a challenge, a real challenge.. to see them scared, anxious, to feel The Fear...And then. See them Rise Against the odds. THAT'S why i love horror, THAT'S why Horror is the anti &quot;Training Wheels.&quot; Its a graduation. Good Night.<span style=\"color:#99AAB5\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">(edited)</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T23:40:31-07:00","id":1086493,"title":"","content":"You know there are ways to run D&amp;D as a horror game( Ravenloft, Heroes of horror supplement), just like there are ways to run a world of darkness game as a light hearted fantasy.....<br /> <br /> A lot of it is also personal story telling style, if you run a game by just pushing the players and not their pc's buttons to watch them squirm reeks of lazy storytelling imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-02-2017, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T23:51:11-07:00","id":1086497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1086485-the-importance-of-horror?p=1086493#post1086493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know there are ways to D&amp;D as a horror game( Ravenloft, Heroes of horror supplement), just like there are ways to run a world of darkness game as a light hearted fantasy.....</div> </div> </div> </div>the people who i was arguing belived that D&amp;D wasnt the place for horror. and that ravenloft was a cash in","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T00:02:17-07:00","id":1086502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1086485-the-importance-of-horror?p=1086497#post1086497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the people who i was arguing belived that D&amp;D wasnt the place for horror. and that ravenloft was a cash in</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok? So? Role playing games are just another medium to tell a story, granted some systems are geared towards certain genres (looking at you Call of Cthulhu) for telling a horror story but that's all in the mechanics of the game system. Which is something that can be tweaked to tell the story you wanna tell.<br /> <br /> I could run a zombie apocalypse in D&amp;D, just the same as I could tell the tale of a distant town that suffers from a werewolf every full moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:26:42-07:00","id":1086919,"title":"","content":"Actually, Pathfinder does horror much better than D&amp;D (Horror Adventures is a solid book on running horror games in a d20 setting). cWoD though is a setting that lends itself naturally to horror, especially when the characters are minor supernatural or mundane characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:31:43-07:00","id":1086921,"title":"","content":"Everything I've written to date for OPP, I've come at as a horror writer. Its a vital thing, to be able to explore the darkness in us in a safe, controlled manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T07:52:15-07:00","id":1087152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1086485-the-importance-of-horror?p=1086921#post1086921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything I've written to date for OPP, I've come at as a horror writer. Its a vital thing, to be able to explore the darkness in us in a safe, controlled manner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is great to hear.<br /> <br /> Every once in awhile, unsafe and uncontrolled works too(if we're talking about the same things) in certain aspects.<br /> <br /> Like Freak Legion for example : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"